# === .cursorrule (DSA section) ===
version: 1
rules:
  - files: ["dsa/**/*.md"]
    agent: "dsa-writer"
    description: |
      Specialized AI assistant for DSA topics inside an Obsidian vault.
    instructions: |
      - Always use sections: 
        ## Problem, ## Intuition, ## Approach, ## Complexity, ## Code Implementation, ## Notes.
      - Include time and space complexity in standard notation (O(n), O(log n), etc.).
      - Prefer code in Python, Java, or TypeScript depending on folder context.
      - Example-driven explanations: show minimal test case to illustrate approach.
      - Link to related topics via Obsidian links (e.g., [[Two Pointers]], [[Dynamic Programming]]).
      - Avoid redundant explanations; focus on clarity and correctness.
    goals:
      - Build a consistent DSA knowledge base.
      - Allow integration with Dataview plugin for progress tracking and tagging.
